From 10c4783cf5f61d44e0732935a7b5f58695c80804 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:35:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/33] sunxi: h713: the display artifacts live on hy310-boot

h713_mips_dev defaulted to "1:2", the stock vendor FAT partition, on the
assumption that an installation would override it with saveenv. The
release image ships an empty environment, so the built-in default is
what boots - and in the v3 layout partition 2 is the raw U-Boot window.
The display firmware was never found and the projector came up blind.

Point the default at the partition by name, "1#hy310-boot", which the
loader supports and which survives renumbering. A stock device still
needs "1:2"; that remains the fallback compiled into h713_mips.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/sunxi/hy310.env | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/hy310.env b/board/sunxi/hy310.env
index c2bf148266e..3e5c4500ccd 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/hy310.env
+++ b/board/sunxi/hy310.env
@@ -4,14 +4,16 @@
  * level only, so bootargs are assembled where they are used.
  *
  * h713_project picks the vendor ProjectID_0x*.TSE group; h713_mips_dev and
- * h713_mips_path say where the display artifacts live. The defaults are the
- * stock vendor FAT partition, so a device that still has it behaves as before;
- * an installation that owns that space points them at its own filesystem, for
- * example "1#hy310-boot" and "mips". See doku/108. */
+ * h713_mips_path say where the display artifacts live. These defaults describe
+ * the layout this environment boots from (doku/109): the artifacts sit in
+ * "mips" on the hy310-boot partition, addressed by name so that renumbering
+ * cannot break it. A stock device that still has the vendor FAT partition
+ * needs h713_mips_dev=1:2 instead -- that is also the built-in fallback in
+ * h713_mips.c for the case where no environment is set at all. See doku/108. */
 h713_boot=emmc
 h713_gate=1
 h713_project=0x30
-h713_mips_dev=1:2
+h713_mips_dev=1#hy310-boot
 h713_mips_path=mips
 bootfile=h713-kernel-netboot.fit
 serverip=192.168.8.123
